            <date type="death" when="1967"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Italian pianist, composer, music critic, and, in later life, professor at the Pontificio Istituto di Musica Sacra in Rome. His article "The Tenor Voice in Europe" (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Music and Letters</name> 11, no. 4  [1930]: 318-24), credits his appreciation of tenor <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">John Sullivan</name> to JJ. Carducci contributed his musical setting of JJ’s poem “Alone” to <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Joyce Book</name>. He and Joyce became friends in the 1930s. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
